00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:45.460
Uhm,

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:46.720
you wont regret it.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.260
Reporter: How did you figure you were gonna start
a car company and be successful at it.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.440
Well, i didn't really think

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.200
Tesla would be successful, I thought
we'd most likely fail.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.090
But I thought that, uh, we at least could

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.260
address the false perception that people had,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.980
that an electric car had to be ugly

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.800
and slow and boring, like a golf
cart.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.780
Reporter: But you say you didn't expect the company be successful?

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:07.420
Then why try?

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.800
Elon: If something's important enough,
you should try even if...

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.220
...the probable outcome is failure.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.680
We focus on signal over noise.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:16.540
Um,

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.760
A lot of companies get confused, they
spend money on things that don't

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.440
actually make the product better.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.540
For example, at Tesla,

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:27.580
we've never spent any money on advertising.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:28.940
Um, we, we've--

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.320
put all the money into R&amp;D, and manufacturing  and design,

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.500
to try to make the car as good as possible.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:36.700
Um,

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:37.980
and, uh...

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.340
I think that's...

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.780
that's the way to go.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.530
For any given company just...

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:47.610
keep thinking about 'all these
efforts that people are expending,

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.420
are they resulting in a better product or service?'

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.760
And if they're not, stop those efforts.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.370
When I interview someone,

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.320
to work at the companies, I ask them to tell me about the problems they worked on

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.540
and how they solved them,

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.980
and if someone was REALLY the
person that solved it,

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.381
they'll be able to answer multiple levels,

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:08.740
they'll be able to go down to the brass tacks
and if they won't

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:09.740
they'll get stuck,

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.420
and then you can say 'oh, this
person was not really the person who solved it'

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.420
because anyone who struggles hard with a problem never forgets it.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.480
If you're creating a company --or if you're joining a company--

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:19.980
Uh,

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.900
the most important thing is to,

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:22.700
uh,

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.120
is to attract great people.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.920
So either join a group that's amazing, that you really respect, or

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.600
if you're building a company-- you've gotta gather great people.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.880
I mean all a company is, is a group of people

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.720
that have gathered together to create a product or service.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:37.960
And so depending upon...

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.400
how talented and hard-working that group is,

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.060
and the degree to which they're focused,

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:42.560
uh,

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.340
cohesively in a good direction,

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.320
that will determine the success the
company.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.300
So,

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.900
do everything you can to gather great people,

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.080
ah, if you're creating company.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.820
You gotta make sure that

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.820
whatever you're doing is a great
product or service,

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.300
it has to be really great.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.340
And i go back to what I was saying earlier, where,

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:03.700
uhm,

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:08.320
if you're a new company... I mean unless it's like some new industry or

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.750
or new market that-- if it's an untapped
market,

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:12.300
then,

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:12.860
then,

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:13.700
ah,

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.280
you have...

